details:
player with ownership activates a blueprint that follows a raycast. On placement activation an object in a pool that corresponds to the blueprint is activated and moved to the hit.normal of the blueprint. This works on master end. On visitor with ownership  the corresponding object only arrives at the expected location for 1 tick and then reverts back to the origin of the pool.

if (pools[i].transform.GetChild(j).gameObject.activeSelf == false && count == 0)
                                {
                                    SendCustomNetworkEvent(VRC.Udon.Common.Interfaces.NetworkEventTarget.All, "NetworkSpawn");
                                    pools[i].transform.GetChild(j).localScale = new Vector3(_x, _y, _z);
                                    pools[i].transform.GetChild(j).SetPositionAndRotation(hit.transform.position, Quaternion.Euler(0.0f, _r, 0.0f));
                                    pools[i].transform.GetChild(j).Translate(hit.normal * 1f);

                                }
the Network event is triggering the activation.  and this only occurs if the pooled object is inactive and the bool control is 0. This ensures all pooled objects are not placed and only one is placed once.
